1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,880
Level one. The recruit.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:06,600
You are 24 years old.

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:08,000
You just finished 4 years in the

4
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:10,160
infantry.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,640
The army gave you skills.

6
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:14,680
It took your knees in return.

7
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:15,760
You have a duffel bag and a discharge

8
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:18,440
paper.

9
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:21,240
You have almost nothing else.

10
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:22,880
The civilian world feels slow and soft

11
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:24,560
and strange.

12
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:25,720
You worked at a hardware store for 3

13
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:27,600
months.

14
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:29,000
You almost lost your mind behind that

15
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:31,000
counter.

16
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,720
People asked you about paint colors and

17
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,800
lawn fertilizer.

18
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:36,080
You smiled and pointed them down aisle

19
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:38,640
seven.

20
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:40,000
Inside, something restless clawed at the

21
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:42,520
walls.

22
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,040
You missed the weight of a rifle.

23
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:47,200
You missed the clarity of a mission.

24
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:48,760
You missed knowing exactly what your job

25
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:50,600
was.

26
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:51,560
A guy from your old unit calls you one

27
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,400
night.

28
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:55,160
His name is Briggs.

29
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:58,160
He sounds different now.

30
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:59,800
He sounds like a man making real money.

31
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:01,040
He tells you about a company that hires

32
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:03,000
veterans.

33
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:04,120
They send men overseas to do security

34
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,240
work.

35
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:07,760
The pay is four times what you made in

36
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:09,520
uniform.

37
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:10,760
He gives you a website and a name to

38
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:12,240
drop.

39
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:13,280
You write it on the back of an electric

40
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:15,040
bill.

41
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:16,600
You stare at the ceiling until the sun

42
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,960
comes up.

43
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:19,440
The next morning, you fill out the

44
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:20,880
application.

45
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:22,480
You list your deployments and your

46
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:24,800
weapons quals.

47
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:28,040
You list your clearances, too.

48
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:30,880
You click submit and you wait.

49
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:32,880
2 weeks later, a recruiter calls you.

50
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:35,280
He has a flat voice.

51
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:37,240
He asks short questions.

52
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:39,160
Can you pass a background check?

53
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:41,880
Can you pass a physical?

54
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:43,840
Can you leave the country in 60 days?

55
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:45,400
You say yes to all three without

56
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:47,120
hesitating.

57
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,760
He tells you to fly to North Carolina

58
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:51,560
for an assessment.

59
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:54,000
You pay for the plane ticket yourself.

60
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:56,200
The assessment is 2 days of running,

61
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,960
shooting, and lifting.

62
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:59,160
They watch how you move under a heavy

63
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:00,800
load.

64
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:02,200
They watch how you handle a rifle under

65
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:04,120
stress.

66
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:06,080
They watch whether you panic when men

67
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:08,440
scream in your face.

68
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:10,640
You do not panic.

69
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:12,120
You learned how to not panic a long time

70
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:14,760
ago.

71
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:18,080
40 men show up for the assessment.

72
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:20,600
By the second day, only half remain.

73
00:02:18,080 --> 00:02:22,360
Some quit when their lungs gave out.

74
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:23,959
Some were cut for mouthing off to the

75
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:25,600
cadre.

76
00:02:23,959 --> 00:02:26,880
You kept your head down and did the

77
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:29,800
work.

78
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:33,280
That is the whole secret, you realize.

79
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:35,959
You do the work and you keep quiet.

80
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:38,920
At the end, they hand you a contract.

81
00:02:35,959 --> 00:02:42,080
You sign it without reading every page.

82
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:43,800
The number at the bottom is staggering.

83
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:45,600
It is more than your father made in a

84
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:47,560
year.

85
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:49,200
You are now a private military

86
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:52,840
contractor.

87
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:55,840
Your real career is about to begin.

88
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:57,040
Level two, the static guard.

89
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,400
They fly you to the Middle East on a

90
00:02:57,040 --> 00:03:00,120
chartered plane.

91
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:02,239
You land at a desert airfield at 2:00 in

92
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:04,280
the morning. The air smells like jet

93
00:03:02,239 --> 00:03:05,600
fuel and hot sand.

94
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:06,800
Your first contract is guarding a

95
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:09,320
compound.

96
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:11,680
It is a logistics base outside a city.

97
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:13,000
The base belongs to the US government.

98
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:14,680
The company you work for holds the

99
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:17,160
protection contract.

100
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:18,519
You stand at a gate for 12 hours a day.

101
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:20,760
You check identification against a

102
00:03:18,519 --> 00:03:22,760
printed list. You search vehicles from

103
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:24,640
bumper to bumper. You wave trucks

104
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:26,800
through after checking under them. You

105
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:29,040
use a long mirror on a pole.

106
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:31,400
The heat is a living thing out here. It

107
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:33,000
is 120° by noon.

108
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:34,080
Your gear weighs 40 lb on your

109
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,040
shoulders.

110
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:37,200
Sweat runs down your spine and pools in

111
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:39,400
your boots.

112
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:41,680
Nothing happens for weeks at a time.

113
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:43,440
Boredom is the real enemy on this job.

114
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:45,480
It dulls your reflexes and softens your

115
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:46,640
attention. You fight it with coffee and

116
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:48,560
discipline.

117
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:50,760
You learn the rhythm of the base. You

118
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:52,440
learn which guards sleep on shift. You

119
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:55,320
learn to stay awake when your body begs

120
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:56,600
to stop. The work is simple. The stakes

121
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:58,480
are not.

122
00:03:56,600 --> 00:04:00,600
One car bomb at the wrong gate kills

123
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:02,760
everyone near it. You think about that

124
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:04,520
every time a vehicle slows down.

125
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:05,640
A truck idles too long at your gate one

126
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:07,800
afternoon.

127
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:08,959
Your heart hammers. Your hand drifts to

128
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:11,160
your rifle.

129
00:04:08,959 --> 00:04:13,280
The driver is just lost. He is looking

130
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:14,760
for a different base. You wave him off

131
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:17,200
and breathe again.

132
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:19,000
That is the job in a single moment. Long

133
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:20,120
hours of nothing wrapped around seconds

134
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,519
of terror.

135
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:23,720
You eat dinner with men from all over

136
00:04:21,519 --> 00:04:25,640
the world. There are South Africans and

137
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:27,240
Brits and Fijians here.

138
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:29,720
Most are former soldiers chasing the

139
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:31,120
same paycheck. They tell war stories you

140
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:32,400
half believe.

141
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:34,680
You learn that everyone out here is

142
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:37,560
running from something. A divorce, a

143
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:38,800
debt, a country with no place for them.

144
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,960
You wonder which one you are running

145
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:41,760
from.

146
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:44,080
The contract has rules nobody actually

147
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:45,720
follows. You are told to log every

148
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:47,280
vehicle that enters.

149
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:48,280
Half the drivers slip the guards a few

150
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:49,840
bills.

151
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:51,320
You learn that money moves faster than

152
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:52,480
any rule here.

153
00:04:51,320 --> 00:04:53,720
You take none of it because you are

154
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:56,440
still new.

155
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:58,760
You make $18,000 a month for this. You

156
00:04:56,440 --> 00:05:00,120
send most of it home every payday.

157
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:02,040
You have a girlfriend back home named

158
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:03,360
Rachel. You met her before you ever

159
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,560
joined the army.

160
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:06,640
She waited through your deployments

161
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:07,880
without complaint. She is waiting now,

162
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:09,280
too.

163
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:11,480
You video call her when the connection

164
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:14,400
holds. You tell her the job is boring

165
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:15,840
and safe. The first part is true enough.

166
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:17,080
The second part is a lie to keep her

167
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:18,840
calm.

168
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:20,680
You finish your first contract after 9

169
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:22,880
months. You go home for a month of

170
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:25,640
leave. You marry Rachel in her parents'

171
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:27,680
backyard. Her father shakes your hand.

172
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:29,040
He tells you to be careful. You promise

173
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:31,240
him you will.

174
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:34,160
Then you get on another plane.

175
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:36,120
Level three, the protection operator.

176
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:37,040
You move up to personal security detail

177
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:38,840
work.

178
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:40,040
The job means you protect people instead

179
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:41,840
of buildings.

180
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:43,160
The pay jumps because the risk jumps

181
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:45,280
with it.

182
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:47,040
Your client is a diplomat. He travels

183
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:48,520
through dangerous cities.

184
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:50,320
You ride in an armored truck in a

185
00:05:48,520 --> 00:05:52,000
three-vehicle convoy.

186
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:53,080
You sit in the back with a rifle across

187
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,840
your lap.

188
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:56,320
Your job is to get the principal there

189
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:57,800
alive.

190
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:59,040
The principal is whoever you were paid

191
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:01,400
to protect.

192
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:02,960
You learn to read a road like a hunter.

193
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:05,160
A parked car with a man in it is a

194
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:06,240
threat. A pile of trash might hide a

195
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:08,200
bomb.

196
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:09,480
A motorcycle that follows too long gets

197
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:11,240
your attention.

198
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:12,320
You run drills until they live in your

199
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:13,680
hands.

200
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:15,880
What do you do if the lead vehicle is

201
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:17,800
hit? What do you do if the principal is

202
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:19,240
wounded? What do you do if you are

203
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:21,160
surrounded?

204
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:22,240
You rehearse every answer a thousand

205
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:24,320
times.

206
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:25,760
The rehearsal keeps you alive when it is

207
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:27,600
real.

208
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:28,720
One afternoon, a car cuts hard into your

209
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:30,120
convoy.

210
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:31,360
Your training takes over before your

211
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:32,840
fear does.

212
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:35,080
You push the principal down below the

213
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:37,240
window. Your driver accelerates and

214
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:39,280
threads through traffic. The car turns

215
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:40,919
out to be a confused civilian.

216
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:42,520
Nobody dies that day.

217
00:06:40,919 --> 00:06:43,800
But your hands shake for an hour

218
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:45,600
afterward.

219
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:46,600
You hide them so the younger guys do not

220
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:48,680
see.

221
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:50,000
A team leader who looks weak loses his

222
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:52,400
men.

223
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:54,280
You are 27 now. You are learning that

224
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:55,840
lesson early.

225
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:58,040
Rachel is pregnant with your first

226
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:59,800
child. You watch the ultrasound on a

227
00:06:58,040 --> 00:07:01,200
cracked phone screen.

228
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:03,600
You are sitting in a safe house when you

229
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:06,080
see it. It is a girl.

230
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:07,640
You decide together to name her Emma.

231
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:10,040
You whisper the name to yourself on the

232
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:11,760
long drives. You promise yourself you

233
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:13,480
will be careful for her.

234
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:14,640
But careful is a relative word in this

235
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:16,280
job.

236
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,600
You start putting money into an account

237
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:20,360
just for her.

238
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:22,000
College, you tell yourself. A future, a

239
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:23,680
safe life.

240
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,280
That account becomes the reason you keep

241
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:26,960
saying yes.

242
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:29,200
The diplomat barely looks at you most

243
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:30,760
days. To him, you are furniture that

244
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:32,800
carries a weapon.

245
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:34,240
You memorize his schedule and his habits

246
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:36,240
and his fears.

247
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:37,960
You know which routes he likes. You know

248
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:39,680
which ones you avoid.

249
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:41,080
You stand outside doors while he eats

250
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:43,440
fine meals.

251
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:45,040
You eat a protein bar in truck.

252
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:46,240
One night a crowd gathers near his

253
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:47,920
hotel.

254
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:49,240
You feel the mood shift like a coming

255
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:51,600
storm.

256
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:53,840
You move him out of side door fast. He

257
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:56,000
never even knew there was danger.

258
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:58,480
That is the job done right. It is

259
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:01,160
invisible and complete.

260
00:07:58,480 --> 00:08:02,920
Level four, the shooter.

261
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:04,120
A war breaks out in a country the news

262
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:06,000
ignores.

263
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:07,560
The company wins a contract to support

264
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,240
operations there.

265
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:10,360
They need men who can do more than guard

266
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:12,400
gates.

267
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:15,400
They offer you a spot on a direct action

268
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:17,480
team. The money is enormous.

269
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:19,160
It is more than you ever imagined. The

270
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:20,280
danger is worse than anything you have

271
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:22,480
seen.

272
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:24,600
You say yes because the money will

273
00:08:22,480 --> 00:08:26,080
secure Emma's future.

274
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:27,520
You tell Rachel it is just another

275
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:29,280
security job.

276
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:31,280
She knows you are lying.

277
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:32,360
She stopped asking real questions a year

278
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:33,840
ago.

279
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:37,000
There is a distance growing between you

280
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:39,599
now. You feel it on every call.

281
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:41,360
You cannot fix it from here.

282
00:08:39,599 --> 00:08:43,960
You deploy to a region with no real

283
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:45,920
government. Militias fight over oil and

284
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:47,560
roads and old grudges.

285
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:49,080
Your team clears buildings and escorts

286
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:51,000
supply columns.

287
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:52,240
You kick in doors not knowing what waits

288
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,880
inside.

289
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:55,440
Sometimes it is empty rooms and

290
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:57,480
frightened families.

291
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:58,720
Sometimes it is armed men who want you

292
00:08:57,480 --> 00:09:01,120
dead.

293
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:03,320
You shoot a man for the first time.

294
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:05,680
You had carried a rifle for years. You

295
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:08,760
had never fired it at a person.

296
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:11,839
Now you do it and then you do it again.

297
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:14,400
You tell yourself it is them or you.

298
00:09:11,839 --> 00:09:16,080
Most nights you believe that completely.

299
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:17,240
Some nights you lie on your cot and

300
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:19,440
stare.

301
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:22,080
You think about the faces you have seen.

302
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:23,800
You push the thought into a locked room.

303
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:25,000
That room is somewhere deep inside your

304
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:27,360
chest.

305
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:30,760
You learn that trick back in the army.

306
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:32,480
It works until one day it does not.

307
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:33,680
Your team takes casualties on a bad

308
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:35,640
rotation.

309
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:36,800
A man named Doyle dies next to you in an

310
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:39,440
ambush.

311
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:42,400
He was 23 and from Ohio.

312
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:44,120
He laughed too loud and meant well.

313
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:45,480
You carry his body to the truck under

314
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:47,120
heavy fire.

315
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:48,440
His blood soaks into your sleeve and

316
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:50,960
dries there.

317
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:54,000
You write nothing about it to Rachel.

318
00:09:50,960 --> 00:09:55,800
You come home with money and silence.

319
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,680
Emma is two now.

320
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:59,960
She does not know your face.

321
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:02,240
She cries when you try to pick her up.

322
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:05,800
She reaches for Rachel instead.

323
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:08,080
That hurts more than any wound ever has.

324
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:09,560
You sit in the dark of your living room.

325
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:10,880
You wonder what kind of man you are

326
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:13,040
becoming.

327
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:14,840
You drink more than you used to.

328
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:16,360
You wake at 3:00 in the morning reaching

329
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:18,040
for a rifle.

330
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:19,240
Rachel finds you at the window watching

331
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:21,560
the street.

332
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:23,400
She asks what you are looking for.

333
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:25,240
You cannot answer her.

334
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:26,560
The truth is you are looking for the

335
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:28,440
war.

336
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:31,240
Part of you misses it.

337
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:33,840
That scares you most of all.

338
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:35,640
Then your next contract email arrives.

339
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:37,160
You stop wondering and you pack your

340
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:40,080
bag.

341
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:41,960
Level five, the team leader.

342
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:43,240
After two more rotations, they make you

343
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:44,880
a team leader.

344
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:47,240
You are good at the work.

345
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:49,320
You are also still alive.

346
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:50,920
In this business, staying alive is a

347
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:52,839
qualification.

348
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:55,280
You now lead eight men through hostile

349
00:10:52,839 --> 00:10:57,760
territory. Four are former special

350
00:10:55,280 --> 00:11:00,000
operations soldiers. Four are solid

351
00:10:57,760 --> 00:11:02,320
shooters like you used to be.

352
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:04,920
You are responsible for the mission. You

353
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:07,839
are responsible for their lives, too.

354
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:09,160
That second weight is heavier by far.

355
00:11:07,839 --> 00:11:11,680
You plan routes and rehearse

356
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:14,320
contingencies. You brief the men before

357
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:16,120
every movement. You decide when to push

358
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:18,640
and when to pull back.

359
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:21,160
A bad call gets your people killed. A

360
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:23,640
good call still might.

361
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:24,920
Leadership is mostly carrying fear for

362
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:26,520
other men.

363
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:27,480
They look to you when everything goes

364
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:30,000
wrong.

365
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:31,760
You cannot let them see your own doubt.

366
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,840
So, you swallow it and give clear

367
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:35,000
orders.

368
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:36,160
You keep your voice flat and your hands

369
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,480
steady.

370
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:40,520
Inside, you are screaming.

371
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:42,640
They will never know it.

372
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:45,120
Your team escorts engineers rebuilding a

373
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:48,360
bridge. Insurgents hit you with mortars

374
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:50,600
and small arms. Rounds crack overhead.

375
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:52,160
Dirt jumps around your boots.

376
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:54,280
You coordinate the fight and call for

377
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:57,480
air support. You move your men into

378
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:59,720
cover. You return fire by sectors.

379
00:11:57,480 --> 00:12:02,240
The contractor aircraft arrive. The

380
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:04,280
attackers scatter into the hills. You

381
00:12:02,240 --> 00:12:06,120
lose no one that day.

382
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:07,160
Your men trust you completely after that

383
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:09,120
fight.

384
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:10,880
That trust is the closest thing to

385
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:13,800
family out here.

386
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:16,480
You think about that word, family.

387
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:17,880
It stings more than you expected.

388
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:19,280
You get to know your men better than

389
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:21,880
your own kin.

390
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:24,800
One has a sick mother back in Texas.

391
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:27,200
Another is saving to open a gym someday.

392
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:29,120
You know which ones drink to sleep. You

393
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:31,720
know which ones pray.

394
00:12:29,120 --> 00:12:33,800
You carry their secrets like your own.

395
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:35,120
When one freezes in a firefight, you

396
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:37,240
cover for him.

397
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:38,680
You pull him aside later and rebuild him

398
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:41,960
quietly.

399
00:12:38,680 --> 00:12:44,200
That is what a team leader does unseen.

400
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:46,080
You are 31 years old now.

401
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:47,200
Rachel sends photos of Emma starting

402
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:49,080
school.

403
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:50,200
Emma has a backpack too big for her

404
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:51,360
frame.

405
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,640
You missed her first day of

406
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:55,000
kindergarten.

407
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:56,760
You missed her birthday last month.

408
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,120
You have missed almost everything that

409
00:12:56,760 --> 00:13:00,440
matters.

410
00:12:58,120 --> 00:13:03,160
You tell yourself the money is worth it.

411
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:05,000
The account for Emma is large now. You

412
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:06,720
could stop today and she would never

413
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,760
want for anything.

414
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:10,839
But you do not stop.

415
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:12,360
You tell yourself one more contract will

416
00:13:10,839 --> 00:13:15,560
make it safe.

417
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:17,760
There is always one more contract.

418
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:19,360
Late at night, you are not sure who you

419
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:21,839
are telling.

420
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:23,360
Level six, the site lead.

421
00:13:21,839 --> 00:13:25,760
Your knees and shoulders are wearing

422
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:28,080
out. Years of heavy gear and hard

423
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:30,280
landings add up. Your right shoulder

424
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:32,840
dislocates if you sleep on it wrong.

425
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:36,200
Your knees ache every cold morning.

426
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:38,000
You feel like an old man at 35.

427
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:39,240
The company offers you a management role

428
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,680
at last.

429
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:43,280
You become a site lead on a major

430
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:45,880
project. You run security for an oil

431
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:47,320
facility. It sits in a volatile region

432
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:49,240
near the border.

433
00:13:47,320 --> 00:13:50,920
You manage 40 contractors across

434
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:52,440
rotating shifts.

435
00:13:50,920 --> 00:13:54,040
You design the defensive plan for the

436
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:56,160
whole compound.

437
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:58,280
You decide where the towers go.

438
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:59,760
You decide who mans them.

439
00:13:58,280 --> 00:14:01,320
You set the patrol routes and the

440
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:02,960
response drills.

441
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:04,400
You handle the local guard force the

442
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:05,960
client hired.

443
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:07,880
Some of them are loyal.

444
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:10,080
Some of them are spies.

445
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:11,560
You learn to tell the difference slowly.

446
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:12,960
You watch their eyes and check their

447
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:14,360
stories.

448
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,640
You sit in meetings with the oil

449
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:17,480
executives.

450
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:18,680
They wear clean suits and worry about

451
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:20,840
budgets.

452
00:14:18,680 --> 00:14:22,080
You wear a sidearm and worry about car

453
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:23,880
bombs.

454
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:25,840
You translate their cost concerns into

455
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:27,840
security realities.

456
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:29,920
You tell them where they can save.

457
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:32,640
You tell them where they cannot.

458
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:34,600
You fire men who drink on shift.

459
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:35,920
You promote men who show judgment under

460
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:37,280
pressure.

461
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:38,960
You write incident reports when

462
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:41,800
something goes wrong.

463
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:43,520
You write a great many incident reports.

464
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:46,280
The region heats up.

465
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:48,200
The attacks increase week by week.

466
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:49,320
A truck rams the front gate one morning

467
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:51,400
at dawn.

468
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:52,560
Your towers open fire before it reaches

469
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:54,320
the wall.

470
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:57,400
Your defenses hold.

471
00:14:54,320 --> 00:15:00,120
Your men respond exactly as drilled.

472
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:02,800
The plan you built saves lives that day.

473
00:15:00,120 --> 00:15:04,960
You walk the smoking wreckage afterward.

474
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:06,720
You feel almost nothing.

475
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:08,120
You feel a strange pride mixed with

476
00:15:06,720 --> 00:15:09,520
exhaustion.

477
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:10,839
The client thanks you in a sterile

478
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:12,560
conference room.

479
00:15:10,839 --> 00:15:15,400
They give you a bonus.

480
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:16,960
They ask you to cut costs next quarter.

481
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:18,440
You explain that cutting guards means

482
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:20,720
cutting safety.

483
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:21,920
They nod and smile and cut the budget

484
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:24,880
anyway.

485
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:27,640
The men in suits never truly understand.

486
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:29,680
To them, the dead are a line item.

487
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:31,280
To you, the dead are men you ate

488
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:32,680
breakfast beside.

489
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:36,240
You start to resent the people you

490
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:38,720
protect. You are 35 years old now. You

491
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:40,960
go home twice a year if you are lucky.

492
00:15:38,720 --> 00:15:42,400
Emma is six. She treats you like a

493
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:44,520
visiting uncle.

494
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:45,400
She is polite and a little shy around

495
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:46,960
you.

496
00:15:45,400 --> 00:15:48,400
Rachel and you barely talk about

497
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:49,840
anything real.

498
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:51,040
You sleep in separate parts of the

499
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:52,600
house.

500
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:54,000
You are providing a life you are never

501
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:55,280
present for.

502
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,200
You start to wonder what you are

503
00:15:55,280 --> 00:16:00,360
actually building.

504
00:15:57,200 --> 00:16:01,760
Level seven, the program manager.

505
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:04,480
The company promotes you to program

506
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:06,960
manager. You now run an entire country's

507
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:09,440
worth of contracts. You oversee hundreds

508
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:12,040
of contractors across many sites. You

509
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:13,560
manage budgets in the tens of millions.

510
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:15,680
You report to executives back at

511
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:17,720
headquarters. You negotiate with the

512
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:19,280
host government for access.

513
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:20,880
You negotiate with the client about

514
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:22,400
scope and money.

515
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,520
You sit between the field and the

516
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:25,560
boardroom.

517
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:26,400
Both sides think you do not understand

518
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:28,200
them.

519
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:29,440
You understand both better than they

520
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:32,000
know.

521
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:33,760
You hire and fire team leaders now. You

522
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,839
decide which contracts the company can

523
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:37,600
fulfill.

524
00:16:34,839 --> 00:16:39,320
You decide which jobs are too dangerous.

525
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:40,520
You sign off on operations that could go

526
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:42,680
wrong.

527
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:43,880
Every signature is a gamble with men's

528
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:46,000
lives.

529
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:47,120
When a contractor dies, the call comes

530
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,560
to you.

531
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:51,040
You have made those calls to families

532
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:52,240
before. You will make them again, you

533
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:53,600
know that.

534
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:54,800
You learned how to write those letters

535
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:57,240
years ago.

536
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:58,839
The words never get any easier.

537
00:16:57,240 --> 00:17:00,280
A vehicle carrying your men hits a

538
00:16:58,839 --> 00:17:01,760
roadside bomb.

539
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:03,839
Two of them die.

540
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:05,360
Three are wounded badly.

541
00:17:03,839 --> 00:17:06,520
You fly to the scene and handle the

542
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:07,760
aftermath.

543
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:08,959
You arrange the bodies and the

544
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:11,160
paperwork.

545
00:17:08,959 --> 00:17:12,760
You arrange the silence, too.

546
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:13,839
You sit with the survivors in a field

547
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:15,560
hospital.

548
00:17:13,839 --> 00:17:17,160
You hold the operation together while

549
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:18,680
grieving alone.

550
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:20,880
You write the letters home that night by

551
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:23,120
lamplight. You You tell their wives they

552
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:24,880
died serving something important.

553
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:26,120
You do not tell them what the job really

554
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:28,319
was.

555
00:17:26,120 --> 00:17:30,480
You are 39 years old now.

556
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:32,600
You barely live in the field anymore.

557
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:34,160
You live in offices, on planes, in

558
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:36,600
compounds.

559
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:38,320
Rachel asks you to come home for good.

560
00:17:36,600 --> 00:17:39,840
Emma is 10 now.

561
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,840
She writes you a letter asking the same

562
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:42,760
thing.

563
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:44,560
Her handwriting is careful.

564
00:17:42,760 --> 00:17:46,080
Her words are simple.

565
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:47,280
She asks if you will be there for her

566
00:17:46,080 --> 00:17:48,880
birthday.

567
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:50,040
You read it twice and put it in your

568
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:52,120
pocket.

569
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:53,280
You tell them one more year, just one

570
00:17:52,120 --> 00:17:55,000
more.

571
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:56,280
You have been saying one more year for a

572
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,240
decade.

573
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:59,760
The truth is, you do not know who you

574
00:17:58,240 --> 00:18:01,320
would be at home.

575
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:02,560
The man who left for the hardware store

576
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:04,280
is gone.

577
